{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310857,"nonce":"NGkfs4NiNoODGCRbUId/D8s3yZM=","title":"E0382 use-of-moved-value is a soft warning; the compiler does not enforce move semantics or emit Free at move sites — drop tracking is ...","message":"The compiler **emits E0382 \"use of moved value\" as a Warning, not an\nError** — `compilation.rs:5356` sets\n`severity: diagnostics::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning`. The MIR pipeline\ndoes NOT consult these warnings: there is no IrInstruction::Free\nemitted at \"move sites\", and aliased values continue to work normally\nat runtime.\n\n**Why:** Verified `compilation.rs:5355-5370` emits Warning-only;\n`drop_scope_stack` / `owned_heap_values` in `hir_to_mir.rs` track\nlifetime by scope, not by move events. Reproduced with a test that\nintentionally uses a value after a \"move\" (`var y = x; consume(x);\nconsume(y); consume(x);`) — all three calls return the correct value,\nboth fields readable, no SIGSEGV, no double-free.\n\n**How to apply:** Don't treat E0382 warnings as bug signals when\ninvestigating silent crashes. They're noise from an unfinished\nborrow-checker; the runtime is unaffected. If a Haxe program crashes\nmid-run, look elsewhere first — interface dispatch wrap, field init,\ndrop scope on heap allocations within nested blocks, etc.\n\n**Pre-existing known issue:** \"False positive ownership warnings on\nprimitives\" is logged in bugs_known.md → primitive params like Float\n`dt` trigger spurious E0382. Ignore those.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_ownership_no_enforcement` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}